This repo is used to perform data inspection for EHT/HOPS data products at several pipeline stages. It supports three main data products:

1. Individual fringe files
    These are the output of fourfit from the HOPS pipeline. They contain detailed fringe-fitting results for individual scan/baseline/polarization products. These files will be opened through the eat library and/or inspected externally with HOPS tools such as fplot and fplotpdf.
2. Alist files
    An alist file is a table summary of many fringe files. It can be loaded into a pandas DataFrame for scan-level, baseline-level, polarization-level, and stage-level diagnostics.
3. UVFITS files
    UVFITS files are calibrated and/or averaged visibility datasets used for imaging and downstream analysis. They contain complex visibilities, weights, uv coordinates, time, frequency/channel, and polarization information. The package may expose these data through both array-like structures and pandas DataFrame views for easier analysis.

For each type of file, the package provides the following inspection utilities.

1. Fringe files (Require HOPS tools as described in eat library, i.e. installing and sourcing HOPS)

    a. Inspect amplitude and phase bandpass behavior within individual sub-channels/IFs for a given track, source, baseline, and polarization. Done

    b. Compare phase and amplitude bandpass behavior before and after bandpass correction by loading fringe files from different pipeline stages. Done

    c. Inspect detailed delay-spectrum behavior. Done


2. Alist files

    a. Plot SNR vs. time across pipeline stages to identify scans, baselines, or polarization products degraded by later stages. Done

    b. Plot coherence histograms and use criteria such as high SNR but low coherence to identify suspicious outliers. Done

    c. Plot corrected phase vs. time for each station and all polarizations. Done

    d. Plot MBD vs. time for all polarization products. Done

    e. Plot delay rate vs. time for all polarization products. Done

    f. Plot SBD − MBD vs. time to diagnose inconsistent delay solutions. Done

    g. Summarize delay and delay-rate outliers in table form. Done

    h. Plot RR − RL and LR − LL delay-difference proxies vs. time to check cross-polarization delay behavior. Done

    i. Plot (RR − RL) − (LR − LL) delay vs. time as an internal consistency diagnostic for R-L delay behavior. Done


3. UVFITS files

    a. Inspect amplitude and phase bandpass behavior across the full frequency/channel setup for raw data. Done

    b. Plot amplitude and phase vs. time for channel-averaged data. Done

    c. Plot amplitude vs. uv distance for visibility-domain sanity checks. Done

    d. Compute and plot closure phase vs. time. Done

    e. Compute and plot closure amplitude vs. time. Done